The JRXML file you provided is syntactically correct, and the field names match your Java code perfectly.
However, there is one major hidden issue that causes PDF generation to fail (or produce a blank file) when the data is empty or low-volume.
The Fix: Handle "No Data" Scenarios
By default, if your Java list is empty (i.e., no variances found), JasperReports behaves as "No Pages". It tries to create a PDF with 0 pages, which often crashes the exporter or creates a corrupt file.
You must tell it: "Even if there is no data, please print the Title and Headers."
Updated nwsa_variance.jrxml
